[size=5][b]Boss HP Text[/b][/size]

The boss health bar tells you roughly how much is left. This tells you exactly.

Writes the boss's current and maximum HP straight into the bar — centred, in the game's own
font, shaking with the bar when the boss takes a hit.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Exact [b]current/total[/b] HP, centred inside the boss health bar
[*]Uses the game's own font, so it looks like it shipped with the game
[*]Moves with the bar's damage shake instead of sitting still on top of it
[*]Outlined text, readable against both the boss and mini-boss bar colours
[*]Configurable format, size, colour and outline
[*]Client-side only — costs nothing, syncs nothing, breaks nothing
[/list]

[size=4][b]Why you want it[/b][/size]

Boss HP scales with the number of players. A Spider Crab with 562 HP on your own has 1405 in
a four-player lobby. The vanilla bar can't show you that, so most people never realise it's
happening. This does.

It's also the difference between "about half" and "262 left, one more harpoon".

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5.4.23.x[/url] — the [b]win_x64[/b] build
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[b]1.[/b] Install BepInEx if you haven't. Download [b]BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip[/b] and unzip it
into the game folder so that [b]winhttp.dll[/b] sits next to [b]How to Fish.exe[/b].

[quote]Careful — Steam's folder contains a [i]second[/i] folder of the same name. The game is at
[b]steamapps\common\How to Fish\How to Fish\[/b], not the first one you land in.[/quote]

[b]2.[/b] Launch the game once and quit. This makes BepInEx create its folders.

[b]3.[/b] Drop [b]HowToFish.BossHpText.dll[/b] into:

[code]How to Fish\BepInEx\plugins\[/code]

[b]4.[/b] Launch and fight a boss.

Mod managers work too — the archive mirrors the game folder structure.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Run the game once, then edit:

[code]How to Fish\BepInEx\config\alexandre.howtofish.bosshptext.cfg[/code]

[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] — turn the numbers off without uninstalling
[*][b]Format[/b] — default [b]{0}/{1}[/b]. {0} is current HP, {1} is maximum. Try [b]{0} / {1} HP[/b]
[*][b]FontSize[/b] — points. 0 copies the boss name's size
[*][b]TextColor[/b] — hex, e.g. [b]#FFE9A0[/b]
[*][b]OutlineWidth[/b] — 0 to 1. Set 0 for no outline
[*][b]OutlineColor[/b] — hex
[/list]

[size=4][b]Multiplayer[/b][/size]

Entirely client-side. The maximum HP is already synced to every client by the game itself, so
this reads a value that's there anyway and draws it. Nothing is sent, nothing is patched on
the host.

[b]Players without the mod are completely unaffected.[/b] You can use it in any lobby, and you
don't need anyone else to install it.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

Built and tested against [b]Unity 6000.4.4[/b] with BepInEx [b]5.4.23.5[/b].

It touches exactly one method and adds one text object, so it should sit alongside other UI
mods without trouble. If you already run a pack that displays boss HP beside the bar, you'll
want one or the other — not both.

[size=4][b]Known behaviour[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The numbers appear on the boss's first damage tick, not the instant the bar fades in
[*]At around half HP the text sits across the edge of the fill — that's why it's outlined
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]

Open source, MIT. Bug reports and pull requests welcome.
